<!--Post: 11795--><!--Time: 1111180613-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11795"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 18, 2005 - 1:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think that the hose and jewelery were prized momentos of his &#34;work&#34;. These momentos allow the killer to relive his &#34;work&#34; over and over again.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
