<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11807"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 18, 2005 - 7:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree that the tropies are a reminder of his experiences.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11807-->
<!--Post: 11819--><!--Time: 1111213796-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11819"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 18, 2005 - 10:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I cannot imagine him getting any action as a man, much less a woman. His mementos allowed him to be &#39;intimate&#39; with his victims, long after they were gone.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11819-->
<!--Post: 11850--><!--Time: 1111279583-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11850"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 19, 2005 - 4:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have read psychologists, especially Lunde, who believed that many of these killers could in some cases kill up to a certain age and then burn themselves out. The killers go dormant neve to kill again was the theory.  .  .   <BR> <BR>On the otherhand I wonder if some of these killers like BTK killed and collected momentos for a the purpose of one day being able to stop killing. The idea would be once they got a certain number of momentos in their &#34;treasure chest&#34; they would then stop killing by reliving their crimes through these momentos whenever the &#34;urge&#34; struck them.  .  .   <BR> <BR>Do you think this is possible TD or E ?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11850-->
<!--Post: 11854--><!--Time: 1111280453-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11854"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 19, 2005 - 5:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Like Scott Peterson, Dennis was treated as a girl when he was a child, he hated this about his mother, these things that he kept were as a reminder of the power he now has over the mother, or woman figure. I have yet to understand the big picture of Rader, I d not for one sec. believe he stopped killing.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11854-->
<!--Post: 11877--><!--Time: 1111333312-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11877"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 20, 2005 - 7:41 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have heard of instances where serial killers have been found living a nonkilling life in obscurity. They &#39;grew&#39; out of it. Manson and Lucas were also treated as girls, dressed as girls and sent to school, if my poor memory serves me correctly. How could DR&#39;s Marine father allow his son to be treated that way? Perhaps DR&#39;s father was weak and his mother a dominatrix, so to speak. Or vice versa. Whatever the answer, he substituted other women for his mother. His parent&#39;s pathology needs to be under a microscope. If his mother was the one who did this to him, he may have appeared helpful and caring toward her, but he probably enjoyed the disability that aging has brought to her life. She is weak and he is strong. Caretakers are in always in control. <BR> <BR>I did not know that Scott was treated as a girl. What are parents thinking? That whatever they do will have no ill effects? That would explain the scar tissue built up so emotions and feelings would have no effect on the heart and mind. I imagine that we should all examine our walls and see what purpose/protection they afford and what is sacrificed at the expense of those walls. In those early formative years, such insulation may prevent future insight into one&#39;s condition and prevent them from being able to do self examination: hence, the apprearance of the cold, heartless killer. Those neurological patterns become so ingrained that they cannot be altered.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11877-->
<!--Post: 11896--><!--Time: 1111367907-->
