<!--/Post: 11912-->
<!--Post: 11920--><!--Time: 1111412351-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11920"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 21, 2005 - 5:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Many first born males receive that special treatment. If it goes too far, they do become spoiled brats, selfish, and lustful. It will get them into trouble. I think that mothers do that because they hope that the male child will become the man that their father is not. JMO. Sampson was a mama&#39;s boy, for example. He couldn&#39;t keep it in his pants, lost his hair, and caused the world to collapse upon him, taking many others with him.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
