<!--Post: 11945--><!--Time: 1111442324-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11945"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 21, 2005 - 1:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dear E, <BR> <BR>Would your information about Peterson include the rumors about him possibly killing his ASU girlfriend, who was found in the desert, hastening his unannonced departure from Arizona St. University ? <BR> <BR>Peterson was on a full ride Golf scholarship. One of his ASU teammates was Phil Michaleson. Michaleson stated that Scott was the more talented golfer and that Scott would have had a fantastic career on the PGA tour.  .  .  <BR> <BR>Why would a person give up a full paid college scholarship and a possible million dollar PGA career at the drop of a hat without explanation ? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11945-->
<!--Post: 11946--><!--Time: 1111442428-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11946"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 21, 2005 - 2:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Btw, <BR> <BR>Peterson has a resemblance to Cary Stayner in that both were considered handsome lady&#39;s men.  .  .  I am sure they both used this to their advantage.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11946-->
<!--Post: 11955--><!--Time: 1111447504-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11955"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 21, 2005 - 3:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Scott Peterson was not on a full ride scholarship to ASU. He was able to obtain a partial acholarship to ASU but he never even made the team. It was too laden with talent and he dropped out of ASU after one semester. <BR>Peterson was on the same golf team in high school at University high in San Diego as Mickelson but was two years younger than Phil and Phil hardly remembers him from there. <BR>Peterson went to Cuesta College for two years after dropping out of ASU.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11955-->
<!--Post: 11967--><!--Time: 1111456427-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11967"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brady<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brady<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 21, 2005 - 5:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well it&#39;s one thing to say they were &#34;babied&#34; and another to say they were treated as &#34;girls.&#34;  Seeing that Jackie Peterson gave up a daughter for adoption, it&#39;s easy to understand how/why she may have babied Scott.  <BR> <BR>However, unless you&#39;ve been speaking with Dennis Rader himself, I&#39;m not sure how you can state as fact that he hated his mother for &#34;babying him.&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11967-->
<!--Post: 11973--><!--Time: 1111469857-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11973"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 21, 2005 - 9:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well I guess Court TV got it wrong. They reported Peterson as having a full golf scholarship to ASU.  .  .    <BR> <BR>It has been all over the media that Michaelson and Peterson were HS teammates.  .  .  <BR> <BR>Michaelson did make a statement, I am searching for the source, that Peterson had more talent than he did and would have been a star on the tour.  <BR> <BR>Phil is never going to admit being friendly or knowing Peterson given the heinous crimes Scott has been convicted of this year.  .  .  guilt by association and Phil&#39;s endorsement &#34;sponsors&#34; have kept Phil quiet about Scott.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
