<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12044"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 22, 2005 - 2:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Court TV did get it wrong. ASU officials researched their records thoroughly and found Peterson never made the golf team. Golf Digest also did an investigation into Peterson ever being on the ASU golf team and found it to be untrue. <BR>As for Dennis Rader ever being a cross dresser I highly doubt it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
